sequenceDiagram
    actor User
    participant UI as Dashboard / Chart.js
    participant API as FastAPI
    participant Pipeline as Analyzer
    participant Apple as Apple RSS / Lookup
    participant Prep as Preprocessor
    participant Sentiment as Local RoBERTa (CPU)
    participant Gemini as Gemini Flash-Lite
    participant Validator as Report Validator
    participant Metrics as Metrics Service

    Note over API,Sentiment: Startup: load sentiment model once and reuse it
    User->>UI: Enter app ID or URL, country, review count
    UI->>API: POST /api/v1/analyze
    API->>API: Validate input, credentials, and rate limit
    API->>Pipeline: Start analysis
    Pipeline->>Pipeline: Acquire single-analysis lock

    loop Pages 1-10, sequentially
        Pipeline->>Apple: Fetch recent reviews
        Apple-->>Pipeline: Review records
        Note over Pipeline,Apple: Timeouts and bounded retries
    end
    Pipeline->>Pipeline: Validate records, deduplicate IDs, sample uniformly
    Note over Pipeline: Report actual count and any shortfall
    Pipeline->>Apple: Look up app details
    Apple-->>Pipeline: App name, developer, icon, store URL

    Pipeline->>Prep: Normalize text and emojis, crop oversized text
    Prep-->>Pipeline: Prepared reviews
    Note over Pipeline: Preserve original review text
    Pipeline->>Metrics: Calculate independent rating metrics
    Metrics-->>Pipeline: Average and star distribution
    Pipeline->>Sentiment: Classify reviews in batches
    Sentiment-->>Pipeline: Positive / neutral / negative + confidence
    Pipeline->>Metrics: Calculate sentiment distribution
    Metrics-->>Pipeline: Counts and percentages

    Pipeline->>Prep: Group reviews by sentiment for Gemini
    Prep-->>Pipeline: Negative, positive, and neutral groups
    Pipeline->>Gemini: System instructions + grouped review JSON
    Note over Pipeline,Gemini: Negative reviews support actionable issues<br/>Positive and neutral reviews provide context
    Gemini-->>Pipeline: Issues, priorities, actions, evidence IDs
    Pipeline->>Validator: Validate schema and cited review IDs
    Note over Validator: Only negative reviews support issues<br/>An empty issue list is valid
    Validator-->>Pipeline: Validated insights with original evidence quotes
    Pipeline->>Metrics: Calculate issue frequency, fractions, and coverage
    Metrics-->>Pipeline: Issue metrics using unique review IDs

    Pipeline->>Pipeline: Attach timings, token usage, and warnings
    Pipeline->>Pipeline: Release analysis lock
    Pipeline-->>API: Unified report
    API-->>UI: JSON response
    UI->>UI: Render charts, insights, and review table
    User->>UI: Filter issues or inspect evidence
    UI-->>User: Interactive report

    opt Download report
        User->>UI: Export JSON
        UI-->>User: Download complete report
    end
    Note over UI,API: Reports stay in memory, no database or server-side report storage
